Package: fastsas
Title: Fast 'SAS7BDAT' Reader Backed by Rust
Version: 0.3.4
Authors@R: c(
    person("Tobias", "Kragholm", , "tkragholm@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Evan", "Miller", role = c("ctb", "cph"),
           comment = "ReadStat, from which parts of the bundled 'sas7bdat' crate derive"),
    person("Hoffmann-La Roche", role = "cph",
           comment = "example data from 'pyreadstat', see inst/COPYRIGHTS"),
    person("EPAM Systems", role = "cph",
           comment = "example data from 'Parso', see inst/COPYRIGHTS"),
    person("Authors of the bundled Rust crates", role = c("aut", "cph"),
           comment = "see inst/AUTHORS"))
Description: High-performance reader for 'SAS7BDAT' files. The parsing core is
    implemented in Rust (the 'sas7bdat' crate) and exposed to R via 'extendr'.
    Returns a 'tibble' with column types compatible with 'haven': Date,
    POSIXct, 'hms', character and double.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/tkragholm/sas7bdat-parser-rs
BugReports: https://github.com/tkragholm/sas7bdat-parser-rs/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
Copyright: See inst/COPYRIGHTS for the example data and the code derived
    from ReadStat, and inst/AUTHORS for the Rust crates bundled in
    src/rust/vendor.tar.xz.
Language: en-US
